courses.learning_outcomes:
Upon completing this course, students should:

1) be familiar with the empirical evidence relating to money, inflation and output in developed economies;

2) be able to understand the consequences of monetary policies in real economies.

courses.required_readings:
Reference textbook:
(1) Foundations of International Macroeconomics, Obstfeld and Rogoff, MIT Press 1996;
(2) International Macroeconomics and Finance: Theory and Econometric Methods, Nelson Mark, Wiley-Blackwell, 2001.

courses.learning_outcomes:
Upon completing this course, students are expected to:
1. Gain exposure to major research topics in economic theory;
2. Be familiar with a wide range of theoretical frameworks and research methods;
3. Be prepared for conducting independent research in related areas.
